# hanzi pipeline: downloaded sources and golden renders (regenerable)
tools/hanzi_pipeline/.cache/
build_host*/
tools/math_pipeline/.cache/
build_math*/
build_english*/
# The English pipeline's cache is tracked on purpose: it holds the fetched
# pictograms and the extracted word audio (~26 MB for 480 words), so a fresh
# clone can rebuild the blob without the mdd or network access. Overrides the
# generic `.cache/` rule above. Prune it when words leave the list -- nothing
# in the build does that for you.
!tools/english_pipeline/.cache/
# ...but not the regenerable parts of it. The blob is byte-identical to the
# copy the firmware links (main/assets/english/english_data.bin) and the
# contact sheets fall out of any build, so tracking either just doubles the
# repo for nothing. The fetched pictograms and extracted audio DO stay: those
# are what a fresh clone cannot reproduce without the dictionary and network.
tools/english_pipeline/.cache/english_data.bin
tools/english_pipeline/.cache/preview/
tools/english_pipeline/.cache/search/

# host sim screenshots
*.ppm
